      "captions": [
        "This is Reflex.",
        "Every fix your team verifies becomes training data for a model you own.",
        "Your agent, your model, your memory. One loop."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "chapter": "01 \u00b7 Reproduce",
      "start": 15.9333,
      "duration": 10.1,
      "captions": [
        "First, Reflex replays the incident.",
        "The handler runs in an OS sandbox against four behavior checks.",
        "Two fail. The retry isn't idempotent."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "chapter": "02 \u00b7 Repair",
      "start": 26.0333,
      "duration": 10.533333333333333,
      "captions": [
        "River writes a patch that catches the replay before inventory moves.",
        "Reflex runs it against the same contract.",
        "4 of 4. One order. 15 seconds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s05",
      "chapter": "03 \u00b7 Verify",
      "start": 36.5667,
      "duration": 13.533333333333333,
      "captions": [
        "Nothing trains unless execution proves it.",
        "On 24 practice tasks, River's repairs passed every check on 19.",
        "Add 5 accepted fixes: 24 verified examples, each with provenance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "chapter": "04 \u00b7 Train",
      "start": 50.1,
      "duration": 11.166666666666666,
      "captions": [
        "Then we train our own model.",
        "Qwen3.5-9B, fine-tuned on River.",
        "48 LoRA steps. 122K tokens. A checkpoint we own."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "chapter": "05 \u00b7 Reuse",
      "start": 61.2667,
      "duration": 14.5,
      "captions": [
        "Now the loop closes.",
        "Our UFO extension calls that checkpoint as a tool.",
        "It fixes the stock-replay bug: 2 of 4 \u2192 4 of 4, in 5.7 seconds.",
        "And the trace flows back into Reflex as new experience."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "chapter": "06 \u00b7 Measure",
      "start": 75.7667,
      "duration": 13.5,
      "captions": [
        "We measure it like researchers.",
        "Held-out incidents never touch training. Memory and learned runs get identical inputs.",
        "All three pass 4 of 4. The benchmark saturated, so harder incidents are next."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "chapter": "07 \u00b7 Proof",
      "start": 89.2667,
      "duration": 10.8,
      "captions": [
        "240 tests pass.",
        "The Repository view already runs pytest against patches on local Python code.",
        "And every number here has a receipt in the repo."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "chapter": null,
      "start": 100.0667,
